  Long worms are based on an old computer programming project.  Whether
long worms actually move or not is open to debate.  If there's a free
space by the head of a long worm a segment is added to the head.  If
there isn't a free space by the head of a long worm a segment is removed
from the tail.  So no segment ever moves from the square it's on.

  This may be why you can split a long worm.  Otherwise just staying
away from the head would be perfect protection.  They have a speed of 3
so they're no real threat.  What's interesting is that baby long worms
have a more dangerous attack of 1d6 than long worms do with 1d4.



